{"Cleanup batches log at Error level on the success path and include the full list of IDs, which can flood logs and potentially expose internal record IDs - should use Debug/Info level and avoid logging the IDs, reserving Error for actual failures": 0.9711087346076965, "Cleanup service ticker was reduced from 10 minutes to 1 minute, which will increase DB/file cleanup load and can cause the cleanup loop to run almost continuously if a cycle takes >1m - this change appears unrelated to the MySQL deadlock fix and should be restored to previous cadence": 0.9493623971939087, "Building the SQLite inline ID list with repeated fmt.Sprintf in a loop is O(n\u00b2) in allocations and can become expensive for large batches - should use strings.Builder with strconv.FormatInt to build the IN list efficiently": 0.5857177972793579, "Test case inserts ~40k annotations and uses a 32k batch size, which can make CI slow/flaky without adding much coverage beyond exercising the batch size > SQLite parameter limit path - should reduce dataset while still exceeding 999 parameters (e.g., ~3003 annotations with batch size 1000) and update the test name which incorrectly mentions a specific SQLite version": 0.43704062700271606}